<WikiLayout title="RE:Heads, Please! Updates - Patch Notes & New Content" description="Follow RE:Heads, Please! updates, patch notes, new content and important wiki changes.">
  <article class="page-shell"><h1>RE:Heads, Please! Updates</h1><p class="page-intro">Verified patch notes, new content and important game changes will be organized here.</p>
    <div class="notice"><strong>No verified updates yet.</strong> Entries will be added with their release date and source when available.</div>
    <h2>How the update log will work</h2><p>An update entry belongs here only when its release context and affected feature can be described without guessing. A useful record separates the date, the visible game change, and the Wiki pages that may need review. It should not copy promotional wording or infer balance changes, rewards, rates, or availability that the current game does not confirm.</p>
    <p>The absence of an update entry does not mean that the game has stopped changing. It means this page does not yet have a verified note suitable for publication. Readers should use the live interface for immediate decisions and treat older screenshots, menus, and instructions as historical context until the same behavior is observed again.</p>
    <h2>What to check after an update</h2><ul><li>Open the Codes hub and recheck claims whose working or expired status may have changed.</li><li>Review affected Items, Coins, or Accessories records for name, source, rarity, value, and acquisition differences.</li><li>Revisit guides when controls, menus, requirements, or progression steps no longer match the visible flow.</li><li>Read Tier List criteria again before applying a ranking to newly changed information.</li></ul>
    <h2>Using dates responsibly</h2><p>A page’s “Last Updated” value records when its content or data was reviewed. It is not a promise that every field remained unchanged afterward. When a live screen differs from a dated Wiki statement, use the game for the immediate decision and narrow the review to the affected claim. Recording the exact old and new wording is more useful than replacing it with a broad assumption.</p>
    <h2>Update FAQ</h2><h3>Why are there no patch notes listed?</h3><p>No entry has completed the project’s verification standard. Publishing an empty status is more accurate than inventing a release description.</p><h3>Will database entries change automatically?</h3><p>No. Verified records must be reviewed before changed information is published through the data workflow.</p><h3>Where should I look in the meantime?</h3><p>Use the category hub that matches the question and check the latest in-game information for anything that may have changed.</p>
